          A dual fuel inverter generator solves two problems at once: it produces power clean enough for laptops, CPAP machines, and modern appliances, and it runs on whichever fuel you can actually get during an emergency. That second point matters more than the spec sheet suggests — gasoline disappears from a region within hours of a major storm, while propane tanks sit on pallets outside every hardware store. Here are the six we would spend our own money on, tested on both fuels.
