            2. Gasoline vs Propane: What Actually Changes
          </h2>

          <p>
            Manufacturers publish separate wattage ratings for each fuel, and the gap is real. Propane contains less energy per unit volume delivered to the cylinder than gasoline, so peak output drops. Across our testing the loss averaged about 10%, consistent with published specs.
