                For emergency backup, yes — mostly for availability rather than economy. After a regional storm, gas stations without power cannot pump and lines run for hours, while propane tanks remain on shelves. Propane also stores indefinitely, so a few tanks in the garage represent days of power that never goes stale, unlike gasoline which degrades in 3-6 months.
